LIdar usb port

🔧 To Make the USB Port Fixed (Optional)
Create a udev rule (on your Raspberry Pi):

bash
sudo nano /etc/udev/rules.d/99-rplidar.rules
Add this line (replace 1a86:7523 with your LIDAR's USB vendor/product ID – find it with lsusb):

text
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", SYMLINK+="rplidar"
Then:

bash
sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
sudo udevadm trigger
Now your LIDAR will always be available at /dev/rplidar, regardless of which USB port it's plugged into.

